<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Deidamia II of Epirus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 232 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Deidamia was the last ruler of the Aeacid royal house of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/epirus">Epirus</a>, a daughter of Pyrrhus II. She was killed during a revolt around 232 BCE, murdered in a temple of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/artemis">Artemis</a> at Ambracia, after which the Epirotes abolished the monarchy and formed the Epirote League.</p></div>
